%
% PURPOSE: Current paper defers AC3 (minimality) honestly — "CST
% produces causal-link claims, not causal-explanation claims" —
% but doesn't defend WHY causal-link claims are independently
% meaningful without minimality. A reviewer can ask: "without
% minimality, in what sense is this 'causal attribution' rather
% than just 'correlation'?"
%
% This patch adds one defensive sentence that anchors the legitimacy
% of causal-link claims in their downstream use cases (mitigation
% verification, fuzzing) — both of which need attribution but not
% explanation.
% =====================================================================

